  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for valkey",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for valkey fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-56684: use-after-free in TLS connection handling that could allow an authenticated client to achieve remote\n  code execution using CLIENT KILL (bsc#1272443).\n- CVE-2026-63639: corrupt stream RDB files containing a shared NACK across consumers can lead to remote code execution\n  (bsc#1272442).\n\nChanges for valkey:\n\n- Update to 8.0.10.\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
